  "requestTimestamp": "2026-07-19T01:39:03.743Z",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nAn individual with ₱250,000 gross compensation income in 2024 is not required to file an income tax return, as this amount is within the tax-exempt threshold.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThis is governed by Section 24 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which states that individuals with a taxable income not exceeding ₱250,000 are exempt from income tax.\n\n### Interpretation\nAccording to the tax schedule effective from January 1, 2023, individuals earning not over ₱250,000 are subject to a 0% income tax rate. Furthermore, Section 51-A of the NIRC provides that employees receiving purely compensation income from a single employer, where the income tax has been correctly withheld, are not required to file an annual income tax return.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor an individual earning ₱250,000 in gross compensation income, they will not incur any income tax liability and thus are not obligated to file a return, provided their income is solely from one employer and the correct withholding has been applied. This simplifies compliance for low-income earners, allowing them to avoid the administrative burden of filing a return.",
